  "id": "Compound::DB00945 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Acetylsalicylic Acid appears to be linked to Cyp2c19 through a series of biochemical pathways that involve cytochrome P450 enzymes. The evidence suggests that Acetylsalicylic Acid binds to Cyp2c9, which is involved in the oxidation of various substrates, including limonene and arachidonic acid. This binding may modulate the activity of Cyp2c19, as both Cyp2c9 and Cyp2c19 are part of the same metabolic pathway. Additionally, the indirect evidence from Path 3 indicates that Acetylsalicylic Acid may influence Cyp2c19 through its effects on Cyclooxygenase Inhibitor activity, which in turn could affect the expression or function of Cyp2c19. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Acetylsalicylic Acid may interact with Cyp2c19, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
